Ticket #7: Add the thing
Status: Github Value Determination

Make it work.

Full auto is on. Work without stopping to ask for confirmation. Leave the ticket in this lane while you work, even if other instructions say to move it when work starts: any move starts the next lane's agent. Move it once, when this lane's work is done, to the next lane as instructed above. Not stopping to ask does not mean dropping questions: anything only the user can answer goes in your open questions. Exit only when nothing waits on the user (your final footer shows \`Open Questions: 0\`); otherwise stop with the open questions as the last thing on screen and leave the session open. Finish in this order: move the ticket (when allowed), print your final footer, then message the orchestrator, if one is watching this lane, as your very last action. Nothing but exiting comes after that message."
`;

exports[`assembled prompt: idea > bare 1`] = `
"Instructions:
- When this agent starts, send a message to the orchestrator agent that you have begun your work on ticket N. 
- Fill out the missing details for the ticket in the project tracker. 
- If there are no open questions move the ticket, update the ticket status to 'PRD'. 
- If a branch/worktree has been made, make sure that is noted in the ticket. 
- When this agent ends, send a message to the Orchestrator agent letting them know that you have completed your work. Send your ticket number, current ticket status and next ticket status. Say your session and tab can be closed only if your final footer shows \`Open Questions: 0\`; otherwise tell the orchestrator agent the questions that are open, leave the tab open, and stop with the open questions as the last thing on screen.

